        "identity": {
          "graphId": "2432f22c-5e03-4b80-a757-7233ff346477"
        },
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "# Twilite Primitive Library\n\nPrimitive graphs describe the language. Example graphs speak the language. Templates arrange the language for a purpose.\n\nEach primitive here is its own graph: Meaning, Invariants, Contract, Ports and Relationships, Behavior, Representations, an explicit boundary of what's *not* part of it, and Examples as references out — never demo content folded into the definition itself.\n\n**In progress.** Declaration is the first, establishing the pattern. `topics/twilite-graph-primitives` already has good working content for View, Content, Port, Glyph, Bridge, and Portal, written before this per-primitive shape was decided — migrating those in is the next increment, not a rewrite from scratch. Property, Method, Event, Event Handler, Edge, Node Class, and Edge Class remain unwritten."
        }
      }
    },
